{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>I am not a man of words.</b> I am not practiced in the craft of tongue — rhetoric and its arrangement — to speak before the king." "<b>Also since yesterday.</b> When I was a sojourner in a foreign land." "<b>Also since the day before yesterday.</b> When I was in Pharaoh's house." "<b>Also since You spoke to Your servant.</b> Even though my rational soul was then in the light of the King's countenance, it did not acquire a trained tongue." "<b>For I am heavy of mouth and heavy of tongue.</b> And this happened to me because, my organs of speech being unfit, my heart therefore did not turn to know how to sustain with a word him that is weary (Isaiah 50:4)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:22.042739600Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}